        "development",
        "expense",
        "research"
      ],
      "text": "Research and development expenses include payroll, employee benefits, stock-based compensation expense, and other headcount-related expenses associated with product development. Research and development expenses also include technology development costs, including AI training and other infrastructure costs, third-party development and programming costs, and the amortization of purchased software code and services content."
    },
    {
      "kind": "SEC_HTML_PROSE",
      "node_index_zero_based": 2513,
      "score": 30,
      "matched_terms": [
        "development",
        "expense",
        "research"
      ],
      "text": "Research and development expenses increased $3.0 billion or 10% driven by investments in cloud and AI engineering and Gaming, including the impact of the Activision Blizzard acquisition."
    },
